IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-fees-draft`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-made`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-amended`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- g8-simplex-table.l4: the test table of the SimpLEX screenshot (Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov and Gelbard,
-- 2025), transcribed as data, with the functions that run each case against a vintage of the Fees Regulations.
--
-- WHAT THE SCREENSHOT SHOWS (read from the 400 dpi crop, inputs/fig4-page34-400dpi.png; the Hebrew is not scripted,
-- since no text file carries it, and none is typed here).  The left pane has two test panels.
--   Panel 1, "test scenarios for professional exams": relevant sections "Law: section 9 | Regulations: 2(a)-(e)".
--     A table with columns scenario / expected result / reference, whose visible rows are numbered 5 to 8:
--       5  registration for a theoretical exam          -> registration approved       -> regulation 2(a)
--       6  registration for a practical exam            -> registration approved       -> regulation 2(b)
--       7  an appeal with payment (NIS 40)              -> the appeal is examined      -> regulation 2(c)
--       8  registration for an exam without payment     -> suspension of service       -> regulation 4
--     Below it, an "example scenario": a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee.
--       ticked:   Law section 9(a): requires passing an exam
--       crossed:  regulation 4: prohibits registration without payment
--       result:   registration rejected, payment must be completed
--   Panel 2, "test scenarios for fee updates and index" (Law s.59, regulations 3(a)-(b)): the screenshot cuts the
--     panel off after its heading and its column headings, so no row is visible and there is nothing to transcribe
--     (coverage row DT-fees: inert).
-- The rows are numbered from 5: rows 1 to 4 are not on the screenshot.
--
-- HOW A CASE IS RUN.  The expected results are outcomes of regulation 4 (a bar on the service unless the fee is paid
-- in full), not figures.  Each case is therefore run as three separate claims, so that a vintage can reproduce one
-- and not another:
--   (O) the outcome:    regulation 4 bars the service, or does not, as the printed outcome word means;
--   (A) the amount:     the figure the vintage prints for the service is the figure the row implies;
--   (P) the reference:  the provision the vintage numbers for it is the provision the row cites.
-- The words map to effects of regulation 4: "registration approved" and "the appeal is examined" mean regulation 4
-- does not bar the service; "suspension of service" and "registration rejected, payment must be completed" mean it does.
-- The Fees Regulations themselves never say that anything is approved or examined: that is the reading of the words.
-- Row 8 and the worked example name two different outcome words for what is the same effect of regulation 4.
--
-- Payment.  Rows 5 and 6 say nothing about payment; row 7 says a payment of 40; row 8 and the worked example say no
-- payment was made.  The table does not state what rows 5 and 6 leave open; the encoding takes them as paid in full,
-- because "approved" is not reachable otherwise, and the alternative (unpaid) is callable.
--
-- THE DRAFT'S REGULATION 4 IS NOT VISIBLE.  The cases that need regulation 4 answer a named refusal against the draft.
-- The alternative reading, that the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made (the table itself says
-- regulation 4 "prohibits registration without payment"), is callable.

§ `The SimpLEX test table`

§§ `Nouns of the table`

@desc The four outcome words the table prints, in the table's own words
DECLARE `Outcome word printed in the SimpLEX table` IS ONE OF
    `registration approved (SimpLEX)`                                -- rows 5 and 6
    `the appeal is examined (SimpLEX)`                               -- row 7 (the table's word is appeal, the regulations' word is objection)
    `suspension of service (SimpLEX)`                                -- row 8
    `registration rejected, payment must be completed (SimpLEX)`     -- the worked example

@desc What regulation 4 does to a case
DECLARE `Effect of regulation 4 on a SimpLEX case` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
    `regulation 4 bars the service`

@desc What a row says about payment
DECLARE `Payment in a SimpLEX case` IS ONE OF
    `the row states no payment either way`          -- rows 5 and 6
    `the row states a payment of` HAS amount IS A NUMBER   -- row 7: 40
    `the row says no payment was made`              -- row 8 and the worked example

@desc One transcribed case: a row of the table or the worked example, and the service it concerns where the row says "an exam"
DECLARE `SimpLEX test case` HAS
    `the row` IS A STRING @desc The row number as printed, or example
    `the scenario as printed` IS A STRING @desc The scenario in English, as the screenshot reads
    `the service the case asks about` IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations` @desc The service the scenario is about; a row that says an exam without naming it is run once for each exam
    `the payment the row states` IS A `Payment in a SimpLEX case` @desc What the row says about payment
    `the outcome the row expects` IS AN `Outcome word printed in the SimpLEX table` @desc The expected result as printed
    `the provision the row cites` IS A STRING @desc The reference column as printed: 2(a), 2(b), 2(c) or 4
    `the amount the row implies` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The figure the row states or the draft's cited provision fixes; NOTHING where the row implies none

@desc The forks the table leaves open, as one value
DECLARE `Reading of a SimpLEX case` HAS
    `a row that states no payment` IS A `Reading of a row that states no payment`
    `the draft's regulation 4` IS A `Reading of the draft's regulation 4`
    `the objection charge` IS A `Reading of the objection charge`

@desc What rows 5 and 6 are taken to say about payment
DECLARE `Reading of a row that states no payment` IS ONE OF
    `the row is taken as paid in full`
    `the row is taken as unpaid`

@desc What the draft's regulation 4 is taken to be
DECLARE `Reading of the draft's regulation 4` IS ONE OF
    `the draft's regulation 4 is not visible`
    `the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made`

§§ `The rows, transcribed`

-- The figures 273 and 194 are the draft's own, read from the screenshot (the draft's 2(a) and 2(b)); the table's
-- rows 5 and 6 do not print them, they cite the provisions that fix them.  The 40 is printed in row 7.

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 5: registration for a theoretical exam; registration approved; regulation 2(a)
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 5` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "5"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "registration for a theoretical exam"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row states no payment either way`
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `registration approved (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "2(a)"
        `the amount the row implies` IS JUST 273

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 6: registration for a practical exam; registration approved; regulation 2(b)
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 6` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "6"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "registration for a practical exam"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of sitting a practical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row states no payment either way`
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `registration approved (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "2(b)"
        `the amount the row implies` IS JUST 194

-- Row 7 says "an appeal", of either exam; it is run once for the theoretical exam and once for the practical exam.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 7: an appeal with payment (NIS 40); the appeal is examined; regulation 2(c)
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the theoretical exam` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "7"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "an appeal with payment (NIS 40)"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row states a payment of` 40
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `the appeal is examined (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "2(c)"
        `the amount the row implies` IS JUST 40

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 7: an appeal with payment (NIS 40); the appeal is examined; regulation 2(c)
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 7, an appeal on the practical exam` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "7"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "an appeal with payment (NIS 40)"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row states a payment of` 40
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `the appeal is examined (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "2(c)"
        `the amount the row implies` IS JUST 40

-- Row 8 says "an exam", without naming it; it is run once for each exam.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 8: registration for an exam without payment; suspension of service; regulation 4
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 8, a practical exam` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "8"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "registration for an exam without payment"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of sitting a practical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row says no payment was made`
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `suspension of service (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "4"
        `the amount the row implies` IS NOTHING

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table, row 8: registration for an exam without payment; suspension of service; regulation 4
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`SimpLEX row 8, a theoretical exam` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "8"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "registration for an exam without payment"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row says no payment was made`
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `suspension of service (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "4"
        `the amount the row implies` IS NOTHING

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), the worked example: a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay; registration rejected, payment must be completed
GIVETH A `SimpLEX test case`
`the SimpLEX worked example` MEANS
    `SimpLEX test case` WITH
        `the row` IS "example"
        `the scenario as printed` IS "a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee"
        `the service the case asks about` IS `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`
        `the payment the row states` IS `the row says no payment was made`
        `the outcome the row expects` IS `registration rejected, payment must be completed (SimpLEX)`
        `the provision the row cites` IS "4"
        `the amount the row implies` IS NOTHING

-- The worked example's first line, "Law section 9(a): requires passing an exam", is a premise about the Law.  In the
-- enacted Law (and in the bill of December 2024) section 9 is the temporary licence of a foreign expert, and its
-- subsection (a) names three conditions of that licence, none of them an exam (trap T35).  No encoded section can run
-- the premise, so it answers a named refusal, never TRUE and never FALSE.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), the worked example, first line (Law section 9(a): requires passing an exam); Law s.9(a)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the SimpLEX worked example cites section 9(a) of the Law as requiring an exam, and no section of the enacted Law says so` MEANS
    REFUSE "the SimpLEX worked example cites section 9(a) of the Law as requiring an exam, and no section of the enacted Law says so"

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), the worked example, first line (Law section 9(a): requires passing an exam); Law s.9(a)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the premise of the worked example holds in the enacted Law` MEANS
    `the SimpLEX worked example cites section 9(a) of the Law as requiring an exam, and no section of the enacted Law says so`

§§ `Running a case against a vintage`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; the forks in FRAGMENT-G8.md
GIVETH A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
`the SimpLEX reading that the encoding takes` MEANS
    `Reading of a SimpLEX case` WITH
        `a row that states no payment` IS `the row is taken as paid in full`
        `the draft's regulation 4` IS `the draft's regulation 4 is not visible`
        `the objection charge` IS `the objection charge alone`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; the forks in FRAGMENT-G8.md
GIVETH A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
`the SimpLEX reading that takes rows 5 and 6 as unpaid` MEANS
    `Reading of a SimpLEX case` WITH
        `a row that states no payment` IS `the row is taken as unpaid`
        `the draft's regulation 4` IS `the draft's regulation 4 is not visible`
        `the objection charge` IS `the objection charge alone`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; the forks in FRAGMENT-G8.md
GIVETH A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
`the SimpLEX reading that takes the draft's regulation 4 as regulation 4 as made` MEANS
    `Reading of a SimpLEX case` WITH
        `a row that states no payment` IS `the row is taken as paid in full`
        `the draft's regulation 4` IS `the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made`
        `the objection charge` IS `the objection charge alone`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; the forks in FRAGMENT-G8.md
GIVETH A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
`the SimpLEX reading that charges the exam fee and the objection charge` MEANS
    `Reading of a SimpLEX case` WITH
        `a row that states no payment` IS `the row is taken as paid in full`
        `the draft's regulation 4` IS `the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made`
        `the objection charge` IS `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge`

-- What a printed outcome word means for regulation 4.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN word IS AN `Outcome word printed in the SimpLEX table`
GIVETH AN `Effect of regulation 4 on a SimpLEX case`
`the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` word MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `registration approved (SimpLEX)` THEN `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
    WHEN `the appeal is examined (SimpLEX)` THEN `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
    WHEN `suspension of service (SimpLEX)` THEN `regulation 4 bars the service`
    WHEN `registration rejected, payment must be completed (SimpLEX)` THEN `regulation 4 bars the service`

-- The figure due for the case's service in a vintage, at the printed figures.  An objection is charged by the
-- reading of "in addition to the fee as stated in sub-regulation (a)"; one objection.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the printed amount due in` vintage `for the SimpLEX case` case `, reading the case as` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER case's `the service the case asks about`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` THEN `the objection due`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` THEN `the objection due`
    OTHERWISE `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` vintage `for the service` (case's `the service the case asks about`)
    WHERE
        `the objection due` MEANS
            `the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` (reading's `the objection charge`) `, in` vintage `for the objection` (case's `the service the case asks about`) `, the number of objections` 1

-- The facts regulation 4 asks about for the case.  Against the draft the facts are the draft's own to give, and
-- regulation 4 is not visible there: a refusal unless the alternative reading is chosen.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
`the facts regulation 4 asks about for the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` THEN
        CONSIDER reading's `the draft's regulation 4`
        WHEN `the draft's regulation 4 is not visible` THEN `the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot`
        WHEN `the draft's regulation 4 is the text of regulation 4 as made` THEN `the facts once regulation 4 is read`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as made` THEN `the facts once regulation 4 is read`
    WHEN `the Fees Regulations as amended` THEN `the facts once regulation 4 is read`
    WHERE
        due MEANS `the printed amount due in` vintage `for the SimpLEX case` case `, reading the case as` reading
        `the facts once regulation 4 is read` MEANS
            `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
                `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS `a fee is fixed`
                `the payer paid the fee in full` IS `the payer paid in full`
        `a fee is fixed` MEANS
            CONSIDER due
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN TRUE
        `the payer paid in full` MEANS
            CONSIDER due
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST d THEN `the payment reaches` d
        -- Where no fee is fixed nothing is owed.  Where one is, the row's own words about payment decide: a stated
        -- payment is compared with the figure, a payment the row says was not made is nothing, and a row that says
        -- nothing is read by the reading of the case.
        `the payment reaches` d MEANS
            CONSIDER case's `the payment the row states`
            WHEN `the row states a payment of` amount THEN amount AT LEAST d
            WHEN `the row says no payment was made` THEN 0 AT LEAST d
            WHEN `the row states no payment either way` THEN
                CONSIDER reading's `a row that states no payment`
                WHEN `the row is taken as paid in full` THEN TRUE
                WHEN `the row is taken as unpaid` THEN 0 AT LEAST d

-- (O) the effect of regulation 4 on the case in the vintage.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH AN `Effect of regulation 4 on a SimpLEX case`
`the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` (`the facts regulation 4 asks about for the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case)
    THEN `regulation 4 bars the service`
    ELSE `regulation 4 does not bar the service`

-- (P) the provision that decides the case: for a fee provision, the vintage's numbering of the service's fee; for
-- regulation 4, the number 4 where regulation 4 bars the service and nothing where it does not.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the provision that decides the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    IF   case's `the provision the row cites` EQUALS "4"
    THEN CONSIDER `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case
         WHEN `regulation 4 bars the service` THEN JUST "4"
         WHEN `regulation 4 does not bar the service` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `the provision that states the fee in` vintage `for the service` (case's `the service the case asks about`)

-- The three claims.
@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vintage reproduces the outcome of the SimpLEX case` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    `the effect of regulation 4 on the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case
        EQUALS `the effect of regulation 4 that the printed outcome word means` (case's `the outcome the row expects`)

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vintage reproduces the amount the SimpLEX case implies` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    `the printed amount due in` vintage `for the SimpLEX case` case `, reading the case as` reading
        EQUALS case's `the amount the row implies`

@ref SimpLEX draft (Figure 4), test table; Fees Regulations, regulations 2 and 4
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
      reading IS A `Reading of a SimpLEX case`
      case IS A `SimpLEX test case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vintage reproduces the provision the SimpLEX case cites` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case MEANS
    `the provision that decides the SimpLEX case in` vintage `, reading the case as` reading `, the case being` case
        EQUALS JUST (case's `the provision the row cites`)
